# .env.example -- joosep personal workbench (*FR:Brunel*)
#
# Copy to `.env` beside docker-compose.yml, fill in, then `chmod 600 .env`.
# Owned by the host `dev` user. NEVER committed. Joosep does not receive this
# file -- he receives a container whose environment already holds his own
# credentials.
#
# DERIVED FROM THE COMPOSE `environment:` BLOCK, deliberately.
# Do NOT inherit apex's .env.example: Hopper's read showed it is neither a
# superset nor a subset of what apex actually consumes -- it carries a
# TUNNEL_TOKEN no service receives (a dead cloudflared-sidecar leftover) while
# omitting REPO_URL/SOURCE_REPO_URL/TEAM_NAME, which ride compose defaults.
# The compose file is the contract; this mirrors it.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GitHub: a FINE-GRAINED PAT for Joosep's own account (`JoosepM-565`), scoped to
#   Eesti-Raudtee/HES-integration-tests   (contents: read)
#   Eesti-Raudtee/rumba                   (contents: read)
# and read-only anywhere else. Expand on demand rather than mirroring the 40+
# repos his org teams grant -- the brief found these are the only two he has
# ever committed to, and the whole `hes`-team grant is unexercised.
#
# NOT the PO's org-wide PAT. The entrypoint writes this value into the
# container user's .bashrc in cleartext, and that user is Joosep -- which is
# correct only while the credential is his to hold.
#
# It must NOT carry: workflow scope, packages:write, admin, or write access to
# any repo's default branch (the team must not be able to merge -- he is not in
# `vjs-code-reviewers`, and the team must not exceed its principal).
GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# Atlassian: JOOSEP'S OWN account + API token, not the PO's.
# Attribution lands on him and his own permission scope applies.
# Corollary: his credential sees a DIFFERENT Jira/Confluence slice than the
# PO's, so an empty result from inside this container is not evidence that a
# thing does not exist.
ATLASSIAN_BASE_URL=https://eestiraudtee.atlassian.net
ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=joosep.madar@evr.ee
ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN=...

# ── Optional (defaults in docker-compose.yml are correct for RC) ──────────────

# Leave BLANK to use OAuth at first run -- recommended, and the standard here.
# He already holds a Claude licence and group (ITSD-39589 / ITSD-39591); reuse
# it rather than requesting a new one. Credentials land in the joosep_home
# volume and survive restarts and rebuilds.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Git attribution inside the container.
GIT_USER_NAME=Joosep Madar
GIT_USER_EMAIL=joosep.madar@evr.ee

# Team name. Used for TEAM_NAME, the tmux session, and ~/.claude/teams/<name>/.
# Cheap to change later: volumes are named for the PERSON, so a rename is a
# directory `mv` inside joosep_home, not a volume migration.
TEAM_NAME=joosep

# Repo overrides -- only if pointing at a fork or mirror.
# REPO_1_URL=https://github.com/Eesti-Raudtee/HES-integration-tests.git
# REPO_2_URL=https://github.com/Eesti-Raudtee/rumba.git
# TOOLKIT_URL=https://github.com/Eesti-Raudtee/dev-toolkit.git

# ── Deliberately ABSENT -- do not add ─────────────────────────────────────────
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN / CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#   VJS2 releases to Cloudflare Pages via GitFlow with PR review as the approval
#   gate. This team observes and reports on that gate; it must not be able to
#   pass through it.
# Any HES_ / VJS_ / PONY_ test-user secret
#   The shared root .env holds live test-user secrets on a shared account. Keep
#   it out of this container entirely.
# Any endpoint URL for the Elron/PONY message tooling
#   That tooling can emit into a LIVE railway dispatch system. Commit 39f16a83
#   (2026-08-26) removed the `isTest` toggle and the server now always sends
#   isTest=false, so a flag-based guardrail no longer exists. The as-built
#   guardrail is TEST-ENDPOINT-ONLY ROUTING, and it only holds while the
#   endpoint is NOT configurable from inside the container -- which means never
#   putting it in this file. Do not reference `isTest` anywhere.
